;; The night hold cooks with a furnace it carries (card 2acf52c6): only once safe from the night (roofed or shut in) does it put the furnace down, cook, eat and dig it up again; the sheltered cook is in night-d-test.
;; A bedrock yard x 8..16, z 8..16 with no roof and a bedrock floor: nothing can be dug in, so the night holds exposed. The body carries a furnace,
;; a stone pickaxe, coal and raw beef and is hungry by RCON (food 8, hp 15). Night is needed: the hold only exists while the night waits for dawn.
;; Should-fail (cook): exposed to the night, the furnace is not put down, so the beef is eaten raw and the furnace stays carried, with or without a pickaxe.
{:defaults
 {:tags [:night :survival :get-food :cook]
  :time :night
  :time-why :dawn-decision
  :plot {:height 6}
  :blocks [[:fill [8 -1 8] [16 3 16] "bedrock" :hollow] [:fill [9 -1 9] [15 -1 15] "bedrock"]
           [:set [9 1 9] "torch"] [:set [15 1 15] "torch"]]
  :body {:at [12.5 0 12.5] :settle-s 2}
  :act [[:rcon "effect give $BODY minecraft:hunger 5 243 true"] [:until-effect-gone "hunger" 30]
        [:rcon "damage $BODY 5 minecraft:generic"]
        [:job (jobs.survival.night {})]]
  :limit-s 150}
 :cases
 [{:name "exposed-hold-eats-raw-and-keeps-the-carried-furnace"
   :body {:inventory [["beef" 2] ["coal" 2] ["furnace" 1] ["stone_pickaxe" 1]]}
   :expect [{:event {:source :job :kind :shelter.ate} :within-s 100}
            {:no-event {:source :job :kind :child_ended :data {:slot :cook}} :for-s 20}]
   :after [[:item "furnace" 1]]
   :limit-s 120}]}
